  "description_short": "Community store and café serving Nature's Valley with essentials, light meals, and a friendly local vibe.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into the heart of Nature's Valley, this trading store has been serving locals and visitors for years as the village's essential hub. More than just a convenience store, it offers a small café section where you can grab a bacon and egg roll for breakfast, sandwiches, pies, and decent coffee before heading to the beach or forest trails.\n\nThe shelves stock basics you might need during your stay — groceries, cold drinks, ice creams, and a few local products. It's the kind of place where you pop in for milk and end up chatting to someone about the best swimming spot or where the otters were spotted that morning. The outdoor seating area catches the morning sun, making it a pleasant stop for a quick bite.\n\nWhile it's a no-frills setup and service can be relaxed (this is Nature's Valley, after all), it fills an important role in a village with limited options. Ideal for grabbing supplies, a takeaway breakfast, or simply soaking up the unhurried rhythm of this special coastal pocket along the Garden Route.",
